Implementing a centralized and consistent error handling strategy is key for user experience and debugging. Define custom exception classes and register them with the FastAPI application:

```python
# core/exceptions.py
from fastapi import HTTPException, status

class ResourceNotFound(HTTPException):
    def __init__(self, detail="Resource not found"):
        super().__init__(status_code=status.HTTP_404_NOT_FOUND, detail=detail)

class InvalidRequest(HTTPException):
    def __init__(self, detail="Invalid request"):
        super().__init__(status_code=status.HTTP_400_BAD_REQUEST, detail=detail)
```

In `main.py`, register handlers:

```python
from fastapi.responses import JSONResponse
from core.exceptions import ResourceNotFound, InvalidRequest

@app.exception_handler(ResourceNotFound)
def not_found_handler(request, exc):
    return JSONResponse(status_code=exc.status_code, content={"error": exc.detail})
```

Centralizar el manejo de errores permite una experiencia de usuario coherente y facilita la depuración. Definí excepciones personalizadas y registralas en la app:

```python
# core/exceptions.py
from fastapi import HTTPException, status

class RecursoNoEncontrado(HTTPException):
    def __init__(self, detalle="Recurso no encontrado"):
        super().__init__(status_code=status.HTTP_404_NOT_FOUND, detail=detalle)

class SolicitudInvalida(HTTPException):
    def __init__(self, detalle="Solicitud inválida"):
        super().__init__(status_code=status.HTTP_400_BAD_REQUEST, detail=detalle)
```

En `main.py`:

```python
from fastapi.responses import JSONResponse
from core.exceptions import RecursoNoEncontrado, SolicitudInvalida

@app.exception_handler(RecursoNoEncontrado)
def handler_404(request, exc):
    return JSONResponse(status_code=exc.status_code, content={"error": exc.detail})
```
